Single-connection heap trim: match CFG_MAX_CONNECTIONS=1.

The ancestor pins 8-connection heap sizes explicitly (ENV 4928 / MSG 6880 /
NON_RET 2048), so BLE_CONNECTION_MAX_USER=1 alone changes nothing: the
scatter macros prefer these defines over the auto formulas. A clock talks to
exactly one client, so size them with the SDK auto formulas at n=1:

  ENV     = ((200+4)+(244+4)+(128+4)+(28+4)) * 1              = 616
  MSG     = 256*(1+1) + 80*1 + 96*(2*1+1) + 256 + 256*1       = 1392
  NON_RET = 1024 (auto value for 1 connection)
  DB      = 1024 (unchanged; not connection-scaled)

Retained heap drops 12868 -> 3068, reclaiming ~9800 B of LR_IROM3 (retained
RAM is carved out of the top of the code region). Applied to the build-copy
only; the ancestor submodule is never modified.

--- a/src/config/da14585_config_advanced.h
+++ b/src/config/da14585_config_advanced.h
@@ -108,8 +108,8 @@
 /* Custom heap sizes                                                                                            */
 /****************************************************************************************************************/
  #define DB_HEAP_SZ              1024
- #define ENV_HEAP_SZ             4928
- #define MSG_HEAP_SZ             6880
- #define NON_RET_HEAP_SZ         2048
+ #define ENV_HEAP_SZ             616
+ #define MSG_HEAP_SZ             1392
+ #define NON_RET_HEAP_SZ         1024

 /****************************************************************************************************************/
